----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB SOURCE ACTUALLY IS (read end-to-end before writing native code)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FormField.tsx is an intentionally tiny, PRESENTATIONAL wrapper: a required label, a control slot
(`children`), and exactly one inline message — `error ? <p role="alert"> : hint ? <p> : null`. Its only
hook is React `useId` (label/control association); it issues NO fetch. Therefore the generic per-surface
"loading / empty / stale / offline" chrome DOES NOT APPLY — those are owned by the host form on the web,
and reproducing them here would be invented drift. The honest port reproduces the REAL branches:
  • label (always visible)                          • required → asterisk + a11y "required" suffix
  • error present → error row (role="alert")        • hint present & no error → hint row
  • neither → no message row                        • htmlFor ?? useId() → caller id ?? generated id
  • error strictly hides hint; whitespace-only error/hint collapses to none (React renders "" as nothing)

